  <p>Age is a powerful predictor of homicide victimization. Young adults aged 25–29 face the highest mean homicide rate among males (29.4 per 100,000), followed closely by those aged 20–24 (26.5). The risk curve rises sharply after age 15 and peaks in the mid-to-late 20s before gradually declining.</p>

  <div class="chart-container" style="height: 400px">
